  "statement": "Let $f(x)=\\dfrac{x+1}{x-1}$. Show that $f(f(x))=x$ for $x\\neq 1$.",
  "solution": "$f(f(x))=f\\!\\left(\\dfrac{x+1}{x-1}\\right)=\\dfrac{\\frac{x+1}{x-1}+1}{\\frac{x+1}{x-1}-1} =\\dfrac{\\frac{x+1+x-1}{x-1}}{\\frac{x+1-x+1}{x-1}}=\\dfrac{2x}{2}=x$. Thus $f$ is self-inverse.",
